body: "## Scope and documented goal\nFound on PR #122 head cce917969c1ee5c12432668e9d996ff9df14bd83; this concerns the proposed feature, not a claim about a released version.\n\n[ARCHITECTURE.md](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/cce917969c1ee5c12432668e9d996ff9df14bd83/ARCHITECTURE.md#L681-L695) promises preserved independent edits, retained repeated contenders and explicit resolution. The [canonical feature](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/cce917969c1ee5c12432668e9d996ff9df14bd83/.agents/pm/features/pm-vcs-p7objects.toon) records an ambiguity guard for repeated fields; the equivalent overlapping text case is unguarded.\n\n## Defect\n[mergeTrees](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/cce917969c1ee5c12432668e9d996ff9df14bd83/engine/rewrite.ts#L340-L371) retains inherited conflict units alongside newly produced units. Successive unresolved merges over the same original-base text hunk can therefore carry overlapping ranges.\n\n[resolvePayload](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/cce917969c1ee5c12432668e9d996ff9df14bd83/engine/conflicts.ts#L166-L176) sorts units by start, then splices each using its original start/end into the already-mutated line array. Overlapping replacements can overwrite or partially retain a previous choice. All selected units are subsequently removed, without the ambiguity check provided for fields.\n\n## Executed sanitized reproduction\nExact pinned resolvePayload, in-memory typed object store:\n- Readable projection: header\\nours\\nfooter\\n\n- Two valid text units both cover zero-based range [1,2)\n- Their selected alternatives are one\\ntwo and three\n- Resolve with take=theirs\n\nActual: header\\nthree\\ntwo\\nfooter\\n; no remaining conflict units. Reversing the input unit order produces header\\none\\ntwo\\nfooter\\n, again with no conflicts. The first result combines fragments of two alternative choices.\n\nExpected: refuse an ambiguous overlapping selection or require an explicit consolidated choice; do not silently mark all alternatives resolved after sequential stale-coordinate splicing.\n\nNegative control: disjoint ranges [1,2) and [3,4) correctly produce header\\none\\ntwo\\nmiddle\\nthree\\nfooter\\n and clear selected units.\n\n## Producer path and limits\nA source-backed producer is three sibling branches editing the same base line, followed by successive record-conflicts merges: inherited unit plus new unit share the projection range. This producer path was inspected, not executed as a full Repository integration test. The resolver was executed unchanged with in-memory storage; this is not an end-to-end CLI reproduction. Canonical hash ordering makes actual ordering deterministic but does not make mixed resolution correct.\n\n## Acceptance/regression criteria\n- Full branch/Repository regression with three text contenders, including alternatives of different lengths\n- Detect overlapping selected ranges and handle ambiguous alternatives explicitly before publishing\n- Apply each explicitly resolved region once with sound coordinates; preserve surrounding independent text\n- Retain disjoint-hunk behavior, EOF state, and field ambiguity tests\n- Ambiguity refusal leaves HEAD/index/worktree unchanged\n\nAll-status issues (122 entries across two REST pages), current PR discussions/reviews and canonical feature were checked. No matching issue was found.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-18T08:03:42Z)\n>\n> Fixed in PR #122 at fc0cbd022d66afc0622a224a8b2da58a75745f78; its body now contains Fixes #124. Real Repository regressions execute the three-sibling producer with unequal alternatives, plus distinct-start partial overlaps and coincident zero-width ranges from ordinary edits. --take refuses ambiguous ranges before publication; --value replaces each connected region once without stale-coordinate splices. Surrounding/disjoint text, all historical alternatives and EOF choices are checked, as are unchanged HEAD/index/disk/mode/merge-state/operations on refusal. Test: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^collapsed text|^three sibling|^explicit text values\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts. Reverting only resolvePayload fails 0/3; reverting only coalescing fails 0/1 with a duplicated two-line tail. Both full release gates pass 1607/1607 with 100% coverage in every dimension across 66 source files. The issue remains open for review. Additional real-branch regression: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^a final zero-width\" test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts checks adjacent inherited ranges ending at the same EOF boundary after two recorded merges and an ordinary deletion. Only the rightmost region owns the final newline. All ours/theirs/base choices pass; reverting only that EOF-owner guard fails 0/1 with a missing trailing newline. The full conflict suite is now 44/44.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-18T11:01:14Z)\n>\n> Review-round verification on 2e85d73b106556426d158dcf1a881be2cf3afc17: overlapping/coincident contender refusal, connected-region explicit replacement, disjoint ranges and EOF ownership all pass through real repositories. `node --test test/first-class-conflicts.test.ts` contributes 49 passing tests to each full release gate (1,612/1,612 each; all four coverage dimensions at 100% across 66 source files). The collapsed-hunk refusal now also starts with an aged cold index and preserves its exact bytes. Original range/coalescing/EOF proofs and the new cache-publication guard-only revert are recorded in the PR body and PM items. `Fixes #124` remains in the PR body."
